THAT Council direct staff to report back with housing solutions to respond to the crisis of North Vancouver residents facing imminent homelessness, including Travelodge evictees, a Canadian Mental Health Association (CMHA) operated home and others who are unhoused, living in their cars or in the rough – now and in the future; 

AND THAT Council direct staff to provide information and timelines for various housing types that can be built within six to twelve months, such as modular homes, pallet homes, tiny homes, container homes and other prefabricated concepts that have been successful in other cities in the Province; 

AND THAT Council direct staff to:
•	Collaborate with BC Housing, Provincial and Federal Governments to determine what funding or grants are immediately available for transitional or temporary housing;
•	Determine if previously approved partnership developments with BC Housing that have not broken ground (Lloyd Street for example) could be used to meet this urgent need; 
•	Determine what Federal Government properties could possibly be used, such as a Canada Post office site; and, 
•	Expedite all permits and development processes required.

