WHEREAS the District recognizes the need for accountability and transparency of Metro Vancouver’s management of the North Shore Wastewater Treatment Plant (NSWWTP) project;

WHEREAS North Shore residents have been burdened with a disproportion share of the cost overruns and have faced project delays and ongoing uncertainty associated with the NSWWTP project;

THEREFORE BE IT RESOLVED THAT the District of North Vancouver Council submit a complaint to the Inspector of Municipalities of British Columbia regarding Metro Vancouver’s management of the NSWWTP, pursuant to section 765 of the Local Government Act (“the Act”); 

AND THAT the complaint specifically requests:

1.	A public inquiry into the NSWWTP cost overruns, to restore public confidence and establish an independent record of what occurred;
2.	A provincial review of Metro Vancouver’s governance framework, particularly the mechanisms by which it can borrow billions on behalf of member municipalities without their meaningful consent; and
3.	A fairness mechanism to protect municipalities from bearing the cost of massive, uncontrolled escalations on regional mega-projects over which they have no effective oversight.

